1
00:00:06,634 --> 00:00:12,102
What is it like, from the inside, when the
habit of making things solid falls quiet?

2
00:00:12,926 --> 00:00:18,118
That habit has a name: reification,
turning what appears into fixed,

3
00:00:18,198 --> 00:00:22,357
separate things. When it is
pacified, something remains.

4
00:00:22,437 --> 00:00:24,436
An old formulation names it.

5
00:00:24,516 --> 00:00:27,697
It comes from the Bahiya
sutta, in the Udāna.

6
00:00:27,777 --> 00:00:29,912
In the seen, only the seen.

7
00:00:29,992 --> 00:00:32,144
In the heard, only the heard.

8
00:00:32,970 --> 00:00:35,064
These words are sometimes misread.

9
00:00:35,144 --> 00:00:40,078
Some take them to reduce experience
to isolated flashes of sense.

10
00:00:40,158 --> 00:00:43,995
Others take them to describe
a blank. Neither reading fits.

11
00:00:44,806 --> 00:00:49,441
The words name a taste. Seeing is
just seeing. Hearing is just hearing.

12
00:00:49,521 --> 00:00:51,819
No seer stands behind the seeing.

13
00:00:51,899 --> 00:00:54,115
No hearer stands behind the hearing.

14
00:00:54,195 --> 00:00:57,838
The gap between observer and
observed was a designation,

15
00:00:57,918 --> 00:01:01,126
a label laid over immediate experience.

16
00:01:01,206 --> 00:01:04,146
It was never found in
the experience itself.

17
00:01:04,957 --> 00:01:10,407
When the labelling stops, experience has a
vividness that is hard to put into words.

18
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:13,101
Colours are vivid. Sounds are immediate.

19
00:01:13,190 --> 00:01:15,927
Thoughts lose their heavy
sense of being owned.

20
00:01:16,758 --> 00:01:21,692
This taste is a sign. It marks that the
reifying habit has been seen through.

21
00:01:21,772 --> 00:01:27,167
It is not a higher stage on a path, and
it is not an attainment. It is recognised.

22
00:01:27,247 --> 00:01:30,496
And the moment one tries to
keep it as an accomplishment,

23
00:01:30,576 --> 00:01:32,348
the fixing has returned.

24
00:01:33,178 --> 00:01:35,272
The witness shows the difference.

25
00:01:35,352 --> 00:01:39,688
If the witness is a separate
subject standing behind experience,

26
00:01:39,768 --> 00:01:44,498
it becomes one more svabhāva, one
more thing with a nature of its own.

27
00:01:44,578 --> 00:01:48,533
If it is simply the vivid,
unobstructed quality of the flow,

28
00:01:48,613 --> 00:01:53,035
then nobody is doing the tasting,
and nobody is doing the seeing.

29
00:01:53,833 --> 00:01:56,429
Nor is the taste a denial of the world.

30
00:01:56,509 --> 00:01:59,826
The seen is still seen.
The heard is still heard.

31
00:01:59,906 --> 00:02:02,317
Nothing has been taken out of experience.

32
00:02:03,125 --> 00:02:06,577
What has gone is an addition:
a viewer, and a ground.

33
00:02:06,657 --> 00:02:11,758
And with them, the sense that experience
is happening to someone, from somewhere.

